00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:40.140
really good plan, a really good piece of advice to&nbsp;
give you, but if it doesn't fit your context, then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:44.700
it's actually not great advice for your particular&nbsp;
situation, whereas questions are very adaptable.&nbsp;

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:48.240
I think maybe what I should do is just go&nbsp;
through some of the questions that I like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:52.440
to ask myself for my annual review&nbsp;
and throughout the rest of the year.&nbsp;

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:58.800
I guess we could say this first category is just&nbsp;
questions that help improve self-awareness or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:03.360
help bring me back to center. The first thing,&nbsp;
and I think actually this might be a question&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:09.600
from Derek Sivers or some version of it from him,&nbsp;
"Just what am I optimizing for?" Sometimes people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:13.860
