larger scale than most people would've done.&nbsp;
So let's take podcasts, for example. Doing a&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:33:06.660 --> 01:33:10.680
podcast tour for your book is a very popular,&nbsp;
typical thing to do when your book comes out.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:33:11.940 --> 01:33:17.460
We put together a list. So I went through&nbsp;
iTunes and I clicked on every category of shows&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:33:18.060 --> 01:33:22.440
that we felt like could be relevant to&nbsp;
the book. So health and fitness, business,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:33:23.340 --> 01:33:26.340
et cetera, and went all the way through. For each&nbsp;
of those categories, I think usually iTunes lists&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:33:26.340 --> 01:33:31.080
like a hundred shows or so in each category.&nbsp;
So we went through all the hundred for each of&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:33:31.080 --> 01:33:36.180
those categories, and then we identified every&nbsp;
show that was already an interview show. So I&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:33:36.180 --> 01:33:40.200
