02:02:23.460 --> 02:02:28.920
if I had to pick a topic that I feel like is more&nbsp;
important than I realized when I was writing the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:02:28.920 --> 02:02:34.560
book, I would probably say this, and that's the&nbsp;
power of the social environment. We are all part&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:02:34.560 --> 02:02:39.960
of multiple tribes. Sometimes, those tribes are&nbsp;
large, like what it means to be American. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:02:39.960 --> 02:02:44.700
sometimes, they're small, like what it means to&nbsp;
be a neighbor on your street or a member of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:02:44.700 --> 02:02:50.280
local gym. But all of those tribes that you belong&nbsp;
to, the large groups and the small groups, they&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:02:50.280 --> 02:02:55.560
all have this set of expectations. They've got a&nbsp;
set of social norms for what you do when you're&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:02:55.560 --> 02:02:59.820
in that group and what the typical way is to act&nbsp;
and behave and what kind of habits they follow.&nbsp;

02:02:59.820 --> 02:03:08.460
And the more that your habits go with the grain of&nbsp;
the expectations of the group, the more attractive&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:03:08.460 --> 02:03:11.880
they feel like to you, because it's like, "Hey,&nbsp;
I fit in. I belong. I'm part of something."&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:03:12.480 --> 02:03:17.760
And the more that they go against the grain of the&nbsp;
expectations of the group, the harder they are to&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:03:17.760 --> 02:03:22.440
stick to, especially in the long run. Maybe you&nbsp;
can do it for a day or a week or, I don't know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:03:22.440 --> 02:03:27.180
a month or two, but at some point, you kind of&nbsp;
keep rubbing against, you have this friction where&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:03:27.180 --> 02:03:32.700
you're conflicting with the group. And it becomes&nbsp;
hard to stick to that for the long run. And so,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:03:32.700 --> 02:03:39.780
the little takeaway that I kind of think of&nbsp;
now is you want to join groups, to join tribes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:03:39.780 --> 02:03:45.060
where your desired behavior is the normal&nbsp;
behavior. Because if it's normal in that group,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:03:45.060 --> 02:03:53.040
then it becomes really motivating to stick to it.
And furthermore, the kind of ancillary habits that&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:03:53.040 --> 02:03:56.760
are part of that group, the other expectations,&nbsp;
are things that you're probably going to soak up.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:03:58.200 --> 02:04:03.120
